honk-core built with the mydist direct hand-back patch (p1).

Direct-classified flows return TC_ACT_UNSPEC and carry DIRECT_UNSPEC_MARK, so the
classic TC chain (mydist's dpd) sees them and can keep accelerating direct
traffic while honk proxies the rest. Proxy and block verdicts remain terminal for
honk, and NAT stays with einat on the WAN.

Absence of this file means an unpatched core: dpd must stay in observe while honk
owns the LAN TCX, because its direct exits return TC_ACT_OK and the classic chain
is never reached.
